From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 07:52:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: let wcnss_filter hold a wakelock

The BT HCI relay runs as bluetooth with group wakelock and sepolicy already says
wakelock_use(wcnss_filter), but /sys/power/wake_lock also demands CAP_BLOCK_SUSPEND
and the service never asked init for it. Every wcnss_acquire_wakelock/release
pair failed EPERM (about one a second, ~1000 log lines per 20 minutes) and BT traffic
could not keep the SoC awake.
---
 rootdir/init.qcom.rc | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rootdir/init.qcom.rc b/rootdir/init.qcom.rc
index ceba47e..96d1aea 100644
--- a/rootdir/init.qcom.rc
+++ b/rootdir/init.qcom.rc
@@ -231,6 +231,8 @@ service start_hci_filter /vendor/bin/wcnss_filter
     class late_start
     user bluetooth
     group bluetooth oem_2950 system wakelock
+    # /sys/power/wake_lock needs CAP_BLOCK_SUSPEND (the wakelock group alone is EPERM)
+    capabilities BLOCK_SUSPEND
     disabled
     writepid /dev/cpuset/system-background/tasks
 
